{"type":"message","id":"f589c7c3","parentId":"5c82ba0b","timestamp":"2026-02-12T17:37:00.547Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-02-12 19:37 GMT+2] Think of yourself as the CEO of the project \"SEOIndicator.com\". Your goal is to improve it. Do not ask me what to do next. Work autonomously.\nFollow the steps:\n\n- Check in `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\TODO.md` for a task to pick up and do it. After successfully completing remove the task from the file.\n\n- If there is no task, then read `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\PROJECT.md` and think of a beneficial task on how to improve the functionality of \"SEOIndicator.com\", update `PROJECT.md` accordingly and respectively `TODO.md`.\n\n- Update `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\AUTO-DEVELOP-LOGS.md` appending 1 line at the end of file with timestamp and concisely what task you will do/are doing or finished doing.\n\n- Follow always Test Driven Development process:\n\n    -- Create automated test\n    -- Develop code\n    -- Run automated tests locally and check if passed, if no then fix\n    -- Git pull & git push to prod\n    -- Check if automated tests passed successfully\n\n- Append to `C:\\Users\\Raitis\\.openclaw\\workspace\\MEMORY.md` critical self improvements if any encountered."}],"timestamp":1770917820545}}
